%abc-2.1
% CONTROL — the NINE places a slur mark can sit, which no fixture in either corpus writes
% and which the `parseOnly` gate could therefore not defend. abcjs numbers a slur at its
% CHORD POSITION — 0 on the element, p+1 on a head, 20 on a grace — so the same `(` gives
% the label 1, 101, 201 or 2001 depending on WHERE it was written, and a close that finds
% its own position empty takes any other or invents one.
%
% Goldens generated by running abcjs 6.7.0 at {staffwidth: 670}.
X:1
T:slur two notes
L:1/4
M:4/4
K:C
(CD)|

X:2
T:slur round a chord
L:1/4
M:4/4
K:C
([CE]G)|

X:3
T:slur inside a chord
L:1/4
M:4/4
K:C
[(CE)G]|

X:4
T:nested slurs
L:1/4
M:4/4
K:C
((CD)E)|

X:5
T:grace slur
L:1/4
M:4/4
K:C
{(CD)}E|

